// parity-expected-stdout-begin
// 7
// 100
// parity-expected-stdout-end

// A constrained function inside a module, called from outside it with an
// instance the module cannot see.
//
// `SoleInstance.measure<a: Sized>` reads `size` out of the `Sized`
// dictionary it is given. `Sized<Int>` is the only instance in its module, and
// this file adds `Sized<String>`; the second call must use it.
//
// History: the old dispatch path saw the sole instance and called
// `__tc_Sized_Int_size` directly, so the second call failed with E1004 (a
// `String` at the `size(x)`). Fixed in 0.0.8 plan step 1e: lowering takes the
// dictionary from the solver's evidence (LLVM from C2), and the VM compiles
// module members from that lowering (C3b).

import SoleInstance

instance Sized<String> {
    fn size(s) { 100 }
}

fn main() with IO {
    print(SoleInstance.measure(7))
    print(SoleInstance.measure("abc"))
}
